Patch 6001: export the registered guest thread contexts so the port can print guest call stacks. (Upstream candidate.)

ppu_report_guest_lrs() prints only each thread's last direct call site. To read a thread's call chain the port needs the context
itself; g_resv_ctxs is file-static. This adds a read-only accessor, used by the port's JSP_THREADDUMP_MS diagnostic.

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
@@ -920,6 +920,13 @@
     long i = _InterlockedExchangeAdd(&g_resv_ctx_n, 1);
     if (i < PPU_RESV_MAX) g_resv_ctxs[i] = c;
 }
+/* i-th registered guest thread context (registration order), or null past the end. Read-only diagnostics. */
+extern "C" ppu_context* ppu_resv_ctx_at(long i)
+{
+    long n = g_resv_ctx_n; if (n > PPU_RESV_MAX) n = PPU_RESV_MAX;
+    if (i < 0 || i >= n) return 0;
+    return g_resv_ctxs[i];
+}
